<title>ITALY: Iraq sees deal with China on Ahdab field.</title>
<headline>Iraq sees deal with China on Ahdab field.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iraqi Oil Minister Amir Muhammed Rasheed said on Thursday that Iraq expected to sign a deal with China soon on development of the Ahdab oil field.  </p>
<p>Asked whether a deal on Ahdab was imminent, Rasheed said &quot;We expect (so), yes.&quot;</p>
<p>He told a news conference in Rome that Iraq also expected to sign a deal with France in the near future but gave no details.</p>
<p>In March Rasheed signed a deal in Baghdad with Russian Fuel and Energy Minister Pyotr Rodionov to develop seven to eight billion barrels of oil reserves in the Southern Iraq Qurana oilfield. Rasheed had said then that the deal would be implemented over 23 years.</p>
<p>--Rome newsroom +39 6 678 2505</p>
